<%#
# Flash Partial

This partial renders flash messages on every page, as banners in the style of
the operator app (tinted surface, matching outline, no emoji).

## Relevant Helpers:

- `flash`:
  Returns a hash,
  where the keys are the type of flash (alert, error, notice, etc)
  and the values are the message to be displayed.

Flash values are plain text and are always escaped; they cannot carry markup.
Error messages built from user input are safe to put in a flash. A message that
needs a link belongs on the page itself, not in a flash.
%>
<%
  flash_tones = {
    'notice' => 'bg-n-teal-2 text-n-teal-11 outline-n-teal-4',
    'success' => 'bg-n-teal-2 text-n-teal-11 outline-n-teal-4',
    'alert' => 'bg-n-amber-2 text-n-amber-11 outline-n-amber-4',
    'error' => 'bg-n-ruby-2 text-n-ruby-11 outline-n-ruby-4'
  }
  fallback_tone = 'bg-n-slate-2 text-n-slate-12 outline-n-weak'
%>

<% if flash.any? %>
  <div class="flashes flex flex-col gap-2 px-4 pt-5 sm:px-7">
    <% flash.each do |key, value| -%>
      <div class="flash flash-<%= key %> rounded-xl px-4 py-2.5 text-left text-sm outline outline-1 -outline-offset-1 <%= flash_tones.fetch(key.to_s, fallback_tone) %>" role="<%= %w[alert error].include?(key.to_s) ? 'alert' : 'status' %>"><%= value %></div>
    <% end -%>
  </div>
<% end %>
